Insertion Sort:-
• Takes one element at a time and places it in its correct position in the already sorted part of the array.
• Selects the current element and compares it with the elements on its left.
• Continues shifting (or swapping) larger elements to the right until the correct position is found.
• Sorts the array while reading the elements, instead of sorting after reading all elements.

Steps for Insertion Sort:
• Assume the first element is already sorted.
• Pick the next element from the unsorted portion.
• Compare it with the elements on its left.
• Shift (or swap) all larger elements one position to the right.
• Insert the current element into its correct position.
• The sorted portion grows by one element after every pass.
• Repeat the process until all elements are inserted into their correct positions.



#include<iostream>
using namespace std;

void insertion_sort(int arr[] , int n){
    for(int i=0; i<=n-1;i++){
        int j = i;
        while(j > 0 && arr[j-1] > arr[j]){
            int temp = arr[j-1];
            arr[j-1] = arr[j];
            arr[j] = temp;



            j--;
        }
    }
}
int main(){
    int n;
    cin>>n;
    int  arr[n];
    for(int i = 0; i<n ; i++){
        cin>>arr[i];
    }
    insertion_sort(arr , n);
    for(int i =0; i<n; i++){
        cout<<arr[i]<<" ";
    }
  return 0;
}

Time Complexity:-
Best case : O(n)
Worst case : O(n²)
